(3780159, 526786, 70369, '<td valign="top">score - 5<br/> <br/>This is somewhat of a stretch for me regarding the challenge, but I don''t mind a stretch if the outcome is better then average.. I think you could have gotten away with a tighter crop, maybe focusing on the line up to the gentleman in the brown shirt.. It still would have shown the line &amp; it would have made it a bit more intimate.. And, there would have been less to distract the eye.. :-)<br/> <br/>The white''s seem pretty blown out so I''m guessing this was the mid part of the day and it was a very grey sky or overcast.. I find that I always seem to shoot at the wrong time of day and using the "s" curve really can help that.<br/> <br/>I do love images of people who don''t seem to realize their picture is being taken and you did a great job at capturing that.. I think if you added a small thin black border, then it would have done this justice and finished it off.. <br/> <br/>Nice job on the focusing and maybe just a touch more of sharpness this would have been a 6.. Overall, you met the challenge and turned in a nice capture!! Keep up the nice work.. :-)<br/> <br/>This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.</td>', 'score - 5 This is somewhat of a stretch for me regarding the challenge, but I don''t mind a stretch if the outcome is better then average.. I think you could have gotten away with a tighter crop, maybe focusing on the line up to the gentleman in the brown shirt.. It still would have shown the line & it would have made it a bit more intimate.. And, there would have been less to distract the eye.. :-) The white''s seem pretty blown out so I''m guessing this was the mid part of the day and it was a very grey sky or overcast.. I find that I always seem to shoot at the wrong time of day and using the "s" curve really can help that. I do love images of people who don''t seem to realize their picture is being taken and you did a great job at capturing that.. I think if you added a small thin black border, then it would have done this justice and finished it off..  Nice job on the focusing and maybe just a touch more of sharpness this would have been a 6.. Overall, you met the challenge and turned in a nice capture!! Keep up the nice work.. :-) This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.', '2007-06-13 20:33:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3780172, 529168, 70369, '<td valign="top">Score 7..<br/> <br/>Now, isn''t this little guy a cutie.. I''ve never seen this type of bird &amp; have no idea what it is, but congrats on submitting a very unique image.. <br/> <br/>I love the dof here.. I think it''s perfect for a subject like this &amp; really helps to show the detail in the feathers.. I''m not a huge fan of the coloring as I don''t feel the orange is adding to the red in the front of the bird or in it''s eye.. It''s sorta competing imho.. <br/> <br/>You have really nice focus and I think that''s perfect as any more sharpening would maybe make this look like it was "too" sharpened.. <br/> <br/>My only gripe would be that some of the feathers on top &amp; side are cut off.. I''m sure it wasn''t easy though capturing this.. Otherwise, it''s a solid entry and one I enjoyed very much.. Keep up the great work !!<br/> <br/>This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.</td>', 'Score 7.. Now, isn''t this little guy a cutie.. I''ve never seen this type of bird & have no idea what it is, but congrats on submitting a very unique image..  I love the dof here.. I think it''s perfect for a subject like this & really helps to show the detail in the feathers.. I''m not a huge fan of the coloring as I don''t feel the orange is adding to the red in the front of the bird or in it''s eye.. It''s sorta competing imho..  You have really nice focus and I think that''s perfect as any more sharpening would maybe make this look like it was "too" sharpened..  My only gripe would be that some of the feathers on top & side are cut off.. I''m sure it wasn''t easy though capturing this.. Otherwise, it''s a solid entry and one I enjoyed very much.. Keep up the great work !! This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.', '2007-06-13 20:38:21.000000', NULL, 1),
