(3786974, 526150, 75478, '<td valign="top">hi man<br/>tnks for commenting.. thought id return the fav... <br/>you got 182/288.. beat you by 150ish :) <br/> <br/>i think a different time of day would help this shot out a bit.. around sunrise/set.. with some richer colors.<br/> <br/>also.. i dont know about the little bit of road you got in on the left side of the photo.. maybe adjusting you position could help out the composition.<br/> <br/>other an that.. keep shooting.. <br/> <br/>Rome wasnt built in a day :)</td>', 'hi mantnks for commenting.. thought id return the fav... you got 182/288.. beat you by 150ish :)  i think a different time of day would help this shot out a bit.. around sunrise/set.. with some richer colors. also.. i dont know about the little bit of road you got in on the left side of the photo.. maybe adjusting you position could help out the composition. other an that.. keep shooting..  Rome wasnt built in a day :)', '2007-06-15 02:11:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3786975, 524544, 62787, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by anahory:</b></div><hr/><i> this photo is a fraud!breast palpation does not substitute mammography and this kind of message is misleading!<br/>(by the way who would want to steal this snapshot?...don ´t put such a rude advise!) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This comment is a personal attack which is entirely misguided. Regarding the first part - the photo encourages early self-examination rather than putting people off mammograms, that seems reasonably obvious to me. As for the second part - how rude! Just who do you think you are? Actually, no, wait, don''t answer that. Please.<br/> <br/>Great photo Leroy :) Don''t let anyone tell you otherwise.</td>', 'Originally posted by anahory: this photo is a fraud!breast palpation does not substitute mammography and this kind of message is misleading!(by the way who would want to steal this snapshot?...don ´t put such a rude advise!)   This comment is a personal attack which is entirely misguided. Regarding the first part - the photo encourages early self-examination rather than putting people off mammograms, that seems reasonably obvious to me. As for the second part - how rude! Just who do you think you are? Actually, no, wait, don''t answer that. Please. Great photo Leroy :) Don''t let anyone tell you otherwise.', '2007-06-15 02:11:37.000000', NULL, 0),
